# Copy to .env and uncomment ONE mode. .env is git-ignored: never commit a real key.
# The three LLM_* variables select the model endpoint. You can also export them
# in your shell instead (the shell wins over .env). With no LLM_BASE_URL at all, Klar. runs in
# replay mode: recorded Apertus answers, no key, no download (this file, unchanged, gives replay).

# --- Mode 1: on-premise GPU workstation (e.g. RTX 5090), `make run-gpu` -------------------
# Official Apertus 1.5 vLLM image, full multimodal model (text + images). `make run-gpu` uses
# these values by default, so you only need HF_TOKEN, once, for the first weight download
# (the model repo is gated). HF_TOKEN goes to the model server only, never to the app.
# LLM_NAME=swiss-ai/Apertus-v1.5-8B
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://llm-gpu:8000/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=local
# HF_TOKEN=
# After the first download, run fully offline:
# HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1

# --- Mode 2: sovereign Swiss cloud (Phoeniqs / kvant), `make run` ------
# Free Evaluation Plan (1M tokens, 30 days, no credit card): https://documentation.kvant.cloud/maas/
# LLM_NAME=inference-apertus-v15-70b
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://maas.phoeniqs.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=

# --- Mode 2b: CSCS, `make run` ---------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_NAME=swiss-ai/Apertus-v1.5-70B
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.inference.cscs.ch/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=

# --- Mode 2c: Hugging Face Inference Providers, `make run DEMO=0` (outside Switzerland) ---
# Quickest live test. Token from https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens with
# "Make calls to Inference Providers" ticked. Public pages only: requests count as external.
# LLM_NAME=swiss-ai/Apertus-v1.5-70B:featherless-ai
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://router.huggingface.co/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=

# --- Mode 3: CPU-only fallback, text criteria only (llama.cpp + GGUF), `make run-cpu` ----
# LLM_NAME=swiss-ai/Apertus-v1.5-8B
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://llm-cpu:8080/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=local

# --- Optional -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Allow scanning intranet sites on private addresses (10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16). Off by default.
# KLAR_ALLOW_PRIVATE_NETWORKS=1
# Extra host names the web UI may be reached under (when exposed with KLAR_BIND=0.0.0.0).
# KLAR_ALLOWED_HOSTS=klar.intranet.example
# Host port and bind address of the web UI (default 127.0.0.1:8080).
# KLAR_PORT=8080
# KLAR_BIND=127.0.0.1
